  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Make the dough: mix all the dough ingredients in a mixer with a dough hook until smooth. Cover and let rise for about 1 hour in the fridge."
    },
    {
      "text": "Make the filling: heat the olive oil in a pan and fry the chopped onion until golden. Add the garlic, chopped za'atar leaves, sumac, salt and pepper and fry for another minute. Cool."
    },
    {
      "text": "Mix the cheeses in a bowl, add the onion mixture and adjust the seasoning."
    },
    {
      "text": "Preheat the oven to 180°C and line 2 trays with baking paper."
    },
    {
      "text": "Flour the work surface and roll the dough to 2 mm thick. Cut 6 cm rounds and place a teaspoon of filling in the centre of each. Close into half-moons and press firmly with pinches or a fork."
    },
    {
      "text": "Place on the trays, brush with beaten egg and sprinkle with sesame seeds."
    },
    {
      "text": "Bake for 20 minutes until golden. To freeze, freeze unbaked on a tray, then transfer to a box; bake from frozen, adding 5 minutes."
    }
  ],
